      "message": "We strongly expect to synchronize this patch so that we can register a wake-up source for devices such as mice.\n\nAt present, the usbhid doesn\u0027t support the mouse as a wake-up source, and similar issues have occurred with keyboards in the past.\nHowever, the commit \u00273d61510f4eca\u0027 (\"HID: usbhid: enable remote wakeup for keyboards\") fixed this issue.\n\nIn order to support mouse wake-up, we submitted a patch to the Linux open source community last year, but it was rejected.\nPlease refer to the details:\nhttps://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-usb/patch/20230222013944.31095-1-michael@allwinnertech.com/\n\nTherefore, we have to continue using the 5.15 kernel approach and register the wake-up source for mouse devices through vendor hooks.",
